    { "type": "text", "id": "p2_learn", "label": "Pathway 2 you will find", "default": "The existing explanation and universal rules." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "p2_leads", "label": "Pathway 2 leads to", "default": "Why cycling exists." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "p2_limit", "label": "Pathway 2 limitation", "default": "Not every compound needs cycling." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "p2_href", "label": "Pathway 2 URL", "default": "#why-cycling" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "p3_title", "label": "Pathway 3 title", "default": "How to track a week" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "p3_for", "label": "Pathway 3 for", "default": "You want a simple on-day / off-day record." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "p3_answers", "label": "Pathway 3 question", "default": "How do I keep the schedule honest?" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "p3_learn", "label": "Pathway 3 you will find", "default": "The weekly dot-grid method already on this page." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "p3_leads", "label": "Pathway 3 leads to", "default": "The weekly dot-grid method." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "p3_limit", "label": "Pathway 3 limitation", "default": "It is a tracker, not a medical taper." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "p3_href", "label": "Pathway 3 URL", "default": "#dot-grid" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "p4_title", "label": "Pathway 4 title", "default": "Off-day options already listed" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "p4_for", "label": "Pathway 4 for", "default": "You want a daily-friendly option on a planned off-day." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "p4_answers", "label": "Pathway 4 question", "default": "What does this guide suggest instead of an empty off-day?" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "p4_learn", "label": "Pathway 4 you will find", "default": "The off-day playbook cards already on this page." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "p4_leads", "label": "Pathway 4 leads to", "default": "The off-day playbook." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "p4_limit", "label": "Pathway 4 limitation", "default": "These options do not replicate a strict-cycle compound." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "p4_href", "label": "Pathway 4 URL", "default": "#off-day-playbook" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Related guide" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "related_heading", "label": "Related heading", "default": "Need dose, timing, or food notes?" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "related_body", "label": "Related body", "default": "Cycling sets which days are on-days. The Dosing Guide lists dose and timing for products that have those notes stored." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "related_cta", "label": "Related CTA", "default": "See dosing guidance" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Hero" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "Reference Guide" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Page heading (H1)", "default": "Cycling Guide" },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "subtitle",
      "label": "Subtitle",
      "default": "<p>Know which compounds need off-days, which need periodic breaks, and which are fine daily — plus a simple tracker to keep your schedule honest.</p>"
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "author", "label": "Author", "default": "Nootropix Research" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "date_published", "label": "Published date (YYYY-MM-DD)", "default": "2026-07-17" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "read_time", "label": "Read time", "default": "14 min read" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Trust badges" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "badge_1_text", "label": "Badge 1", "default": "Scheduling, not medical advice" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "badge_2_text", "label": "Badge 2", "default": "Tier-based" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "badge_3_text", "label": "Badge 3", "default": "Pairs with Dosing Guide" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Why cycling" },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "why_cycling",
      "label": "Why cycling exists",
      "default": "<p>Cycling means scheduling planned off-days or off-weeks instead of taking a compound continuously. The reason is tolerance. With repeated daily exposure to certain compounds, your nervous system adapts: receptors become less responsive, and the same dose produces less effect. The usual reaction is to take more. That accelerates the adaptation and, for some compounds, raises the stakes considerably.</p><p>Off-days give that adaptation time to reverse. A well-planned cycle may help you maintain response at the same dose over months instead of weeks. In our experience, the most common reason people say a nootropic stopped working is not the compound or the batch. It is the schedule.</p><p>Not everything needs cycling. Part of using nootropics well is knowing which tier each compound sits in. That is what this guide is for.</p>"
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Tier intros" },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "tier1_intro",
      "label": "Tier 1 intro",
      "default": "<p>These build tolerance quickly with frequent use. The schedule is not optional. If you only apply this guide to one tier, make it this one.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "tier2_intro",
      "label": "Tier 2 intro",
      "default": "<p>Slower tolerance curves. These reward run-and-rest blocks rather than strict weekly limits.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "tier3_intro",
      "label": "Tier 3 intro",
      "default": "<p>These do not need cycling. Some actively work better with consistent daily use.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "tier3_list",
      "label": "Tier 3 compound list",
      "default": "<p>L-Theanine, Lion's Mane, Cordyceps, Bacopa Monnieri, Ashwagandha KSM-66, choline sources (Alpha-GPC, CDP-Choline, Choline Bitartrate), ALCAR, N-Acetyl L-Tyrosine, Taurine, GABA, Agmatine, Magnesium, Vitamin D3 + K2, and phosphatidylserine.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "tier3_note",
      "label": "Tier 3 note (Bacopa / Lion's Mane)",
      "default": "<p><em>Two of these deserve a special note:</em> Bacopa and Lion's Mane build their effects over weeks of daily use. Cycling them is counterproductive. If a compound belongs in this tier, taking days off does not protect anything; it just delays the benefit.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "stacks_note",
      "label": "Stacks note",
      "default": "<p><strong>Stacks and bundles:</strong> a stack inherits the strictest cycling rule of any compound inside it. If a stack contains a Tier 1 compound, the whole stack follows Tier 1 scheduling.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "peptides_note",
      "label": "Peptides note",
      "default": "<p>Peptides are not covered here. Research peptides follow different protocols and constraints entirely and are outside the scope of this guide.</p>"
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Phenibut deep-dive" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "phenibut_title", "label": "Title", "default": "Phenibut, specifically" },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "phenibut_body",
      "label": "Body",
      "default": "<p>Phenibut is our most popular compound and the one where scheduling matters most. It acts on GABA-B signaling, and the nervous system adapts to that kind of input quickly when it arrives daily. Held to 2-3 non-consecutive days per week, most people report a consistent response over long stretches. Used daily, tolerance can build within weeks, and stopping abruptly after extended daily use can be genuinely unpleasant.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "phenibut_signs",
      "label": "Reset signs list",
      "default": "<p><strong>Signs your schedule needs a reset:</strong></p><ul><li>The dose that used to work no longer does</li><li>You find yourself using it more days per week than you planned</li><li>Off-days feel noticeably rough rather than simply ordinary</li><li>You are using it to feel normal rather than to support a specific day</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "phenibut_taper",
      "label": "Taper note",
      "default": "<p>If any of these apply, the answer is a longer break, not a higher dose. If you have been using Phenibut daily for an extended period, do not stop abruptly on your own. Talk to a clinician about tapering. That is outside the scope of a scheduling guide, and it matters.</p>"
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Dot-grid method" },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "dot_grid_intro",
      "label": "Dot-grid intro",
      "default": "<p>The simplest cycling tracker we know. One row per week, one dot per day:</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "dot_grid_steps",
      "label": "Dot-grid steps",
      "default": "<ol><li>Draw seven circles in a row, Monday through Sunday</li><li>Before the week starts, mark your planned on-days for each strict-cycle compound. Filled dot = on-day, empty dot = off-day</li><li>At the end of each day, check reality against the plan</li><li>At the end of the week, count. If your filled dots exceed your plan two weeks running, your schedule has drifted and it is time for a reset break</li></ol><p>The point of planning on-days in advance is that it turns should I take it today? from an in-the-moment decision into a calendar fact. Decisions made in advance are easier to keep.</p>"
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Off-day playbook" },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "playbook_intro",
      "label": "Playbook intro",
      "default": "<p>Off-days work better when they are not empty. These daily-friendly options cover the most common reasons people reach for a Tier 1 compound:</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "playbook_outro",
      "label": "Playbook outro",
      "default": "<p>None of these replicate a Tier 1 compound, and that is the point. The off-day is doing its own job.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "bottle_math",
      "label": "Bottle math",
      "default": "<p>Your bottle is a cycling audit you already own.</p><ul><li>At 2-3 days per week and one capsule per on-day, a 30ct bottle covers roughly 10-15 weeks and a 60ct covers roughly 20-30 weeks</li><li>If a bottle that should last months is emptying monthly, you are not cycling; you are dosing daily. Recount your dots before you reorder</li></ul><p>Higher per-day doses change the math, but the principle holds: the reorder date tells the truth about the schedule.</p><p>This is also why we suggest sizing your order to your protocol rather than defaulting to the biggest bottle. The right count for a cycled compound is the one that runs out on schedule.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "cross_link",
      "label": "Cross-link to Dosing Guide",
      "default": "<p>For per-compound dose ranges, see our <a href=\"/pages/dosing-guide\">Dosing Guide</a>.</p>"
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Structured data" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "emit_breadcrumb_schema", "label": "Emit breadcrumb schema", "default": true },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "emit_faq_schema", "label": "Emit FAQ schema (visible FAQ blocks only)", "default": true },
    { "type": "text", "id": "breadcrumb_parent_label", "label": "Breadcrumb parent label", "default": "Guides" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "breadcrumb_parent_url", "label": "Breadcrumb parent URL", "default": "/pages/guides" },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "og_image", "label": "Article image (optional)", "info": "Used in Article JSON-LD when set." },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "seo_description",
      "label": "SEO description",
      "default": "The Nootropix cycling guide — tier-based scheduling for strict-cycle, periodic-break, and daily-friendly compounds, plus the dot-grid method and off-day playbook."
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Disclaimer" },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "disclaimer",
      "label": "Disclaimer",
      "default": "<p>These statements have not been evaluated by regulatory authorities and are not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease. This guide is educational and is not a substitute for professional medical advice; consult a qualified healthcare professional before use, especially if you are taking medication or managing a health condition. Not for use by anyone under 18, or during pregnancy or nursing. Results vary by individual and goal.</p>"
    },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding_top", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "label": "Padding top", "default": 0 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding_bottom", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "label": "Padding bottom", "default": 48 }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "jump_link",
      "name": "Jump link",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "label", "label": "Label" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "anchor", "label": "Anchor ID (without #)" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "rule",
      "name": "Universal rule",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Title" },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "body", "label": "Body" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "tier1_row",
      "name": "Tier 1 row",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "richtext", "id": "compound", "label": "Compound" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "on_days", "label": "Suggested on-days" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "break_pattern", "label": "Break pattern" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "off_day_pairing", "label": "Off-day pairing" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "tier2_row",
      "name": "Tier 2 row",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "compound", "label": "Compound" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "pattern", "label": "Suggested pattern" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "playbook_card",
      "name": "Playbook card",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Title" },
        { "type": "richtext", "id": "body", "label": "Body" },
        { "type": "product", "id": "product", "label": "Optional product link" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "faq",
      "name": "FAQ",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "question", "label": "Question" },
        { "type": "richtext", "id": "answer", "label": "Answer" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    { "name": "Cycling Guide" }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
